{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:36:02", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2668945f-6c42-465a-aa94-af1c0110fa99', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "project_id": "7b1ad4f4",\n  "task_id": "ee7de405",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix",\n  "specific_issue": "Metrics pane shows reversed cost savings values, with most expensive agent (Opus) appearing as biggest cost improvement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EHu58ycFrRwGX6Y63s8qyE', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EHu58ycFrRwGX6Y63s8qyE', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Management & Cleanup System - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nThe user needs to manage failed agents more effectively and clean up old data to improve system performance. Specifically:\\n1. Retry failed agents automatically, and if they fail again, delete them permanently\\n2. Provide a way to delete old completed jobs\\n3. Address system slowness caused by data accumulation\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\nThe existing system has:\\n- **Recovery system** (`swarm_recovery.py`): Handles agent recovery with multiple strategies (RETRY, ESCALATE_MODEL, ABORT, etc.)\\n- **Swarm state** (`swarm_state.py`): SQLite-backed state management with cleanup_old_data() method\\n- **Backend APIs** (`main.py`): Endpoints for recovery, cleanup, and retention management\\n- **Data retention** (`data_retention.py`): Existing retention management\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Objective 1: Retry Failed Agents with Auto-Delete on Second Failure\\n**Priority: HIGH**\\n\\nCreate a \\"retry and delete\\" feature that:\\n1. Allows user to retry all currently failed agents\\n2. Tracks retry attempts for each failed agent\\n3. Automatically deletes agents that fail a second time after retry\\n4. Shows clear status in the UI of what happened (retried, deleted, succeeded)\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add new API endpoint: `POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed`\\n  - Finds all agents with status = \'failed\' \\n  - Queues each for retry with a \\"delete_on_failure\\" flag\\n  - Returns count of agents queued for retry\\n- Add new API endpoint: `POST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete`\\n  - Retries single agent, deletes if it fails again\\n- Modify recovery system to track \\"second_failure\\" and auto-delete\\n- Add frontend button \\"Retry All Failed (auto-delete on 2nd failure)\\"\\n\\n### Objective 2: Delete Old Completed Jobs\\n**Priority: HIGH**\\n\\nCreate a job cleanup feature that:\\n1. Shows list of old completed jobs/sessions\\n2. Allows bulk deletion by age (e.g., \\"Delete jobs older than 7 days\\")\\n3. Allows individual deletion of specific completed jobs\\n4. Includes confirmation before destructive actions\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add new API endpoint: `DELETE /api/jobs/completed`\\n  - Query params: `older_than_days` (optional), `session_ids` (optional list)\\n  - Deletes sessions and all associated data (agents, messages, events, etc.)\\n  - Returns count of deleted items\\n- Add new API endpoint: `GET /api/jobs/completed/stats`\\n  - Returns count and size of completed jobs, grouped by age\\n- Add frontend component for job cleanup:\\n  - Shows completed jobs with age\\n  - Bulk delete by age slider/dropdown\\n  - Individual delete buttons\\n  - Confirmation modal before delete\\n\\n### Objective 3: Performance Improvements\\n**Priority: MEDIUM**\\n\\nAddress system slowness by:\\n1. Adding database vacuuming after bulk deletes\\n2. Implementing smarter data loading (pagination, lazy loading)\\n3. Adding database size monitoring\\n4. Cleaning up orphaned data\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add `VACUUM` after bulk deletes\\n- Add API to get database size: `GET /api/system/db-stats`\\n- Add cleanup of orphaned records (messages/events without parent agents)\\n- Consider adding index optimizations if needed\\n\\n## Scope Constraints\\n**IN SCOPE:**\\n- Backend API endpoints for the features above\\n- Frontend UI components for retry and cleanup\\n- Modifications to existing recovery system\\n- Documentation updates\\n\\n**OUT OF SCOPE:**\\n- Automatic scheduled cleanup (can be added later)\\n- Archive to external storage (just delete for now)\\n- Undo/recovery of deleted data\\n- Complex data migration\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. User can click one button to retry all failed agents\\n2. Agents that fail twice are automatically deleted\\n3. User can see and delete old completed jobs by age\\n4. System performance noticeably improves after cleanup\\n5. All existing functionality continues to work\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing SQLite database schema\\n- Must not break existing API endpoints\\n- Must be accessible from the existing React frontend\\n- Should follow existing code patterns\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- \\"Failed agents\\" means agents with status = \'failed\' in the database\\n- \\"Completed jobs\\" means sessions with status = \'completed\'\\n- \\"Delete\\" means permanent removal from database (no soft delete)\\n- Performance issues are primarily from data volume, not code issues\\n\\n## Files to Modify/Create\\n\\n### Backend (Python)\\n1. **src/runtime/agents/swarm_recovery.py** - Add retry-and-delete logic\\n2. **src/runtime/agents/swarm_state.py** - Add delete methods\\n3. **src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py** - Add new API endpoints\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n1. **New: src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/JobCleanupPanel.jsx** - UI for job cleanup\\n2. **Modify: RecoveryDashboard.jsx** - Add retry-all-failed button\\n3. **Modify: App.jsx** - Add navigation to cleanup panel\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n1. First: API endpoints for retry-all-failed and delete completed jobs\\n2. Second: Modify recovery system for auto-delete on second failure\\n3. Third: Frontend components\\n4. Fourth: Performance optimizations and testing\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0165q8HFuWR6bRxbe2HgwGDb', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix', 'description': 'Fix metrics pane showing reversed cost savings values - Opus appearing as biggest cost improvement instead of most expensive'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0165q8HFuWR6bRxbe2HgwGDb', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "4d27f759", "message": "Created project: Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix", "summary": {"project_id": "4d27f759", "project_name": "Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix", "description": "Fix metrics pane showing reversed cost savings values - Opus appearing as biggest cost improvement instead of most expensive", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T23:35:18.710530", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T23:35:18.710530", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T23:35:18.710530", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016Fy9ou4Kcy7UMYgPwUgZry', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Milestone Plan: Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix\n\n## Project Overview\n**Issue**: Metrics pane displays reversed cost savings values, showing the most expensive agent (Opus) as having the biggest cost improvement instead of the highest cost.\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\nThe cost savings calculation logic is likely inverted, showing negative values as positive improvements or calculating savings incorrectly relative to a baseline.\n\n## Milestone 1: Identify and Fix Cost Calculation Logic\n**Timeline**: 1-2 hours\n**Priority**: Critical\n\n### Objective\nLocate the metrics calculation code and fix the inverted cost savings logic.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Investigation of current cost calculation implementation\n2. Fixed cost savings calculation logic\n3. Updated metrics display\n4. Validation tests\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Opus (most expensive agent) shows as highest cost, not highest savings\n- [ ] Cost savings values accurately reflect actual cost differences\n- [ ] All agents show correct relative cost positions\n- [ ] Metrics pane displays consistent, logical cost information\n\n### Dependencies\n- Access to frontend metrics component\n- Access to backend cost calculation logic (if any)\n- Understanding of agent pricing model\n\n### Technical Tasks\n1. **Investigation Phase**\n   - Locate metrics calculation code in frontend\n   - Identify cost data source (hardcoded, API, calculation)\n   - Document current calculation logic\n   - Identify the inversion point\n\n2. **Fix Phase**\n   - Correct the cost savings calculation formula\n   - Update display logic if needed\n   - Ensure proper sorting/ordering of agents by cost\n\n3. **Validation Phase**\n   - Test with known agent costs\n   - Verify all agents display correct relative positions\n   - Check edge cases (zero cost, same cost agents)\n\n### Expected Files to Modify\n- Frontend metrics component (likely in React components)\n- Cost calculation utilities (if separate)\n- Potentially backend API if cost calculation happens server-side\n\n### Risk Assessment\n**Low Risk**: This appears to be a straightforward calculation fix with clear expected behavior.\n\n**Mitigation**: \n- Backup existing calculation logic before changes\n- Test thoroughly with multiple scenarios\n- Verify no other components depend on the incorrect calculation\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Opus shows as most expensive agent (highest cost)\n- Cost savings accurately represent actual savings potential\n- All agents ordered correctly by cost impact\n- No regression in other metrics display functionality\n\n## Next Steps After Completion\n1. Commit fixes with clear description\n2. Consider adding validation tests for cost calculations\n3. Document correct cost calculation methodology'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016Fy9ou4Kcy7UMYgPwUgZry', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_233536.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_233536.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FH9krvK3bZGDk9arQUMBxp', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'project_scope': 'Fix metrics pane showing reversed cost savings values - Opus appearing as biggest cost improvement instead of most expensive', 'output_fi