{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 23:36:06", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1241f9a0-7064-470f-acf8-2e84c9c6c12f', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "project_id": "7b1ad4f4",\n  "task_id": "ee7de405",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix",\n  "specific_issue": "Metrics pane shows reversed cost savings values, with most expensive agent (Opus) appearing as biggest cost improvement"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EHu58ycFrRwGX6Y63s8qyE', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EHu58ycFrRwGX6Y63s8qyE', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Agent Management & Cleanup System - Requirements\\n\\n## Vision\\nThe user needs to manage failed agents more effectively and clean up old data to improve system performance. Specifically:\\n1. Retry failed agents automatically, and if they fail again, delete them permanently\\n2. Provide a way to delete old completed jobs\\n3. Address system slowness caused by data accumulation\\n\\n## Current State Analysis\\nThe existing system has:\\n- **Recovery system** (`swarm_recovery.py`): Handles agent recovery with multiple strategies (RETRY, ESCALATE_MODEL, ABORT, etc.)\\n- **Swarm state** (`swarm_state.py`): SQLite-backed state management with cleanup_old_data() method\\n- **Backend APIs** (`main.py`): Endpoints for recovery, cleanup, and retention management\\n- **Data retention** (`data_retention.py`): Existing retention management\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Objective 1: Retry Failed Agents with Auto-Delete on Second Failure\\n**Priority: HIGH**\\n\\nCreate a \\"retry and delete\\" feature that:\\n1. Allows user to retry all currently failed agents\\n2. Tracks retry attempts for each failed agent\\n3. Automatically deletes agents that fail a second time after retry\\n4. Shows clear status in the UI of what happened (retried, deleted, succeeded)\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add new API endpoint: `POST /api/agents/retry-all-failed`\\n  - Finds all agents with status = \'failed\' \\n  - Queues each for retry with a \\"delete_on_failure\\" flag\\n  - Returns count of agents queued for retry\\n- Add new API endpoint: `POST /api/agents/{agent_id}/retry-and-delete`\\n  - Retries single agent, deletes if it fails again\\n- Modify recovery system to track \\"second_failure\\" and auto-delete\\n- Add frontend button \\"Retry All Failed (auto-delete on 2nd failure)\\"\\n\\n### Objective 2: Delete Old Completed Jobs\\n**Priority: HIGH**\\n\\nCreate a job cleanup feature that:\\n1. Shows list of old completed jobs/sessions\\n2. Allows bulk deletion by age (e.g., \\"Delete jobs older than 7 days\\")\\n3. Allows individual deletion of specific completed jobs\\n4. Includes confirmation before destructive actions\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add new API endpoint: `DELETE /api/jobs/completed`\\n  - Query params: `older_than_days` (optional), `session_ids` (optional list)\\n  - Deletes sessions and all associated data (agents, messages, events, etc.)\\n  - Returns count of deleted items\\n- Add new API endpoint: `GET /api/jobs/completed/stats`\\n  - Returns count and size of completed jobs, grouped by age\\n- Add frontend component for job cleanup:\\n  - Shows completed jobs with age\\n  - Bulk delete by age slider/dropdown\\n  - Individual delete buttons\\n  - Confirmation modal before delete\\n\\n### Objective 3: Performance Improvements\\n**Priority: MEDIUM**\\n\\nAddress system slowness by:\\n1. Adding database vacuuming after bulk deletes\\n2. Implementing smarter data loading (pagination, lazy loading)\\n3. Adding database size monitoring\\n4. Cleaning up orphaned data\\n\\n**Technical Requirements:**\\n- Add `VACUUM` after bulk deletes\\n- Add API to get database size: `GET /api/system/db-stats`\\n- Add cleanup of orphaned records (messages/events without parent agents)\\n- Consider adding index optimizations if needed\\n\\n## Scope Constraints\\n**IN SCOPE:**\\n- Backend API endpoints for the features above\\n- Frontend UI components for retry and cleanup\\n- Modifications to existing recovery system\\n- Documentation updates\\n\\n**OUT OF SCOPE:**\\n- Automatic scheduled cleanup (can be added later)\\n- Archive to external storage (just delete for now)\\n- Undo/recovery of deleted data\\n- Complex data migration\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. User can click one button to retry all failed agents\\n2. Agents that fail twice are automatically deleted\\n3. User can see and delete old completed jobs by age\\n4. System performance noticeably improves after cleanup\\n5. All existing functionality continues to work\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must work with existing SQLite database schema\\n- Must not break existing API endpoints\\n- Must be accessible from the existing React frontend\\n- Should follow existing code patterns\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- \\"Failed agents\\" means agents with status = \'failed\' in the database\\n- \\"Completed jobs\\" means sessions with status = \'completed\'\\n- \\"Delete\\" means permanent removal from database (no soft delete)\\n- Performance issues are primarily from data volume, not code issues\\n\\n## Files to Modify/Create\\n\\n### Backend (Python)\\n1. **src/runtime/agents/swarm_recovery.py** - Add retry-and-delete logic\\n2. **src/runtime/agents/swarm_state.py** - Add delete methods\\n3. **src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py** - Add new API endpoints\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n1. **New: src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/JobCleanupPanel.jsx** - UI for job cleanup\\n2. **Modify: RecoveryDashboard.jsx** - Add retry-all-failed button\\n3. **Modify: App.jsx** - Add navigation to cleanup panel\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n1. First: API endpoints for retry-all-failed and delete completed jobs\\n2. Second: Modify recovery system for auto-delete on second failure\\n3. Third: Frontend components\\n4. Fourth: Performance optimizations and testing\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0165q8HFuWR6bRxbe2HgwGDb', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix', 'description': 'Fix metrics pane showing reversed cost savings values - Opus appearing as biggest cost improvement instead of most expensive'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0165q8HFuWR6bRxbe2HgwGDb', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "4d27f759", "message": "Created project: Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix", "summary": {"project_id": "4d27f759", "project_name": "Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix", "description": "Fix metrics pane showing reversed cost savings values - Opus appearing as biggest cost improvement instead of most expensive", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T23:35:18.710530", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T23:35:18.710530", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T23:35:18.710530", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016Fy9ou4Kcy7UMYgPwUgZry', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Milestone Plan: Agent Cost Savings Metrics Fix\n\n## Project Overview\n**Issue**: Metrics pane displays reversed cost savings values, showing the most expensive agent (Opus) as having the biggest cost improvement instead of the highest cost.\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\nThe cost savings calculation logic is likely inverted, showing negative values as positive improvements or calculating savings incorrectly relative to a baseline.\n\n## Milestone 1: Identify and Fix Cost Calculation Logic\n**Timeline**: 1-2 hours\n**Priority**: Critical\n\n### Objective\nLocate the metrics calculation code and fix the inverted cost savings logic.\n\n### Deliverables\n1. Investigation of current cost calculation implementation\n2. Fixed cost savings calculation logic\n3. Updated metrics display\n4. Validation tests\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Opus (most expensive agent) shows as highest cost, not highest savings\n- [ ] Cost savings values accurately reflect actual cost differences\n- [ ] All agents show correct relative cost positions\n- [ ] Metrics pane displays consistent, logical cost information\n\n### Dependencies\n- Access to frontend metrics component\n- Access to backend cost calculation logic (if any)\n- Understanding of agent pricing model\n\n### Technical Tasks\n1. **Investigation Phase**\n   - Locate metrics calculation code in frontend\n   - Identify cost data source (hardcoded, API, calculation)\n   - Document current calculation logic\n   - Identify the inversion point\n\n2. **Fix Phase**\n   - Correct the cost savings calculation formula\n   - Update display logic if needed\n   - Ensure proper sorting/ordering of agents by cost\n\n3. **Validation Phase**\n   - Test with known agent costs\n   - Verify all agents display correct relative positions\n   - Check edge cases (zero cost, same cost agents)\n\n### Expected Files to Modify\n- Frontend metrics component (likely in React components)\n- Cost calculation utilities (if separate)\n- Potentially backend API if cost calculation happens server-side\n\n### Risk Assessment\n**Low Risk**: This appears to be a straightforward calculation fix with clear expected behavior.\n\n**Mitigation**: \n- Backup existing calculation logic before changes\n- Test thoroughly with multiple scenarios\n- Verify no other components depend on the incorrect calculation\n\n## Success Metrics\n- Opus shows as most expensive agent (highest cost)\n- Cost savings accurately represent actual savings potential\n- All agents ordered correctly by cost impact\n- No regression in other metrics display functionality\n\n## Next Steps After Completion\n1. Commit fixes with clear description\n2. Consider adding validation tests for cost calculations\n3. Document correct cost calculation methodology'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016Fy9ou4Kcy7UMYgPwUgZry', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_233536.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260116_233536.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FH9krvK3bZGDk9arQUMBxp', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'project_scope': 'Fix metrics pane showing reversed cost savings values - Opus appearing as biggest cost improvement instead of most expensive', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FH9krvK3bZGDk9arQUMBxp', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 62.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed project completion by thoroughly reviewing the milestone status document, updating project tracking records, and creating comprehensive completion documentation. My approach focu...\n- Executed a comprehensive validation project with systematic approach, leveraging multiple agents to design, implement, and validate the A/B testing framework. Demonstrated ability to drive project fro...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'd