hould be whimsical and fun\n   - Names should not be repetitive (need variety in generation)\n   - Names should be memorable and pronounceable\n\n3. **Technical Requirements**:\n   - Integrate with existing naming system\n   - Maintain backward compatibility\n   - Ensure consistent generation quality\n   - Support configurable name categories/themes\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n- Expanding name databases/sources\n- Enhancing name generation algorithms\n- Adding new thematic categories\n- Testing for variety and appropriateness\n- Documentation updates\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing core naming system architecture (unless necessary)\n- Adding complex AI-generated names (stick to curated sources)\n- Personalization features\n- Name history/favorites functionality\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n1. **Diversity**: Generated names show significantly more variety\n2. **Quality**: All names are family-friendly and whimsical\n3. **Sources**: Names clearly draw from specified domains\n4. **Integration**: System works seamlessly with existing code\n5. **Testing**: Comprehensive testing shows reduced repetition\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n- Must work with existing ensemble UI system\n- Should not break current naming functionality\n- Performance should not degrade significantly\n- Names should load quickly\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- Current naming system exists and is modifiable\n- System uses some form of name database or generation logic\n- Family-friendly means no offensive, scary, or inappropriate content\n- Roman political/military terms will be adapted to be whimsical (e.g., "Consul Giggles")\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. **As a user**, I want to see more varied names so that the experience feels fresh\n2. **As a user**, I want whimsical names that make me smile and are appropriate for all ages\n3. **As a developer**, I want the naming system to be easily expandable with new sources\n4. **As a maintainer**, I want the system to generate consistently high-quality names\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] New name sources implemented and integrated\n- [ ] Name generation shows measurably reduced repetition\n- [ ] All generated names pass family-friendly content review\n- [ ] System maintains existing performance characteristics\n- [ ] Comprehensive test suite validates name quality and variety\n- [ ] Documentation updated with new sources and maintenance procedures'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FLryRS1sqjKgMksAeT3Wcb', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260117_001015.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260117_001015.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RFYWJghjRyBLmZ1owayE1e', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '86b841f9', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Requirements phase complete - documented vision for enhancing naming system with diverse whimsical sources'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RFYWJghjRyBLmZ1owayE1e', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Lp3cFBgZ5BZsVbgwQVwHge', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Lp3cFBgZ5BZsVbgwQVwHge', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Name Enhancement - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Vision**: Enhance the existing naming system to include more diverse, whimsical, and family-friendly names that are less repetitive and draw from multiple creative sources.\\n\\n**Problem**: Current whimsical names are getting repetitive and lack diversity in their sources and styles.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Goal\\nExpand the naming system to generate more diverse and creative whimsical names suitable for family-friendly contexts.\\n\\n### Specific Requirements\\n\\n1. **Name Sources**: Pull terms from multiple creative domains:\\n   - Fantasy literature and mythology\\n   - Science fiction (books, movies, shows)\\n   - Roman politics and military terminology\\n   - Video game characters and terminology\\n   - Other creative sources (animation, comics, etc.)\\n\\n2. **Quality Standards**:\\n   - Names must be family-friendly and appropriate for all ages\\n   - Names should be whimsical and fun\\n   - Names should not be repetitive (need variety in generation)\\n   - Names should be memorable and pronounceable\\n\\n3. **Technical Requirements**:\\n   - Integrate with existing naming system\\n   - Maintain backward compatibility\\n   - Ensure consistent generation quality\\n   - Support configurable name categories/themes\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Expanding name databases/sources\\n- Enhancing name generation algorithms\\n- Adding new thematic categories\\n- Testing for variety and appropriateness\\n- Documentation updates\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Changing core naming system architecture (unless necessary)\\n- Adding complex AI-generated names (stick to curated sources)\\n- Personalization features\\n- Name history/favorites functionality\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Diversity**: Generated names show significantly more variety\\n2. **Quality**: All names are family-friendly and whimsical\\n3. **Sources**: Names clearly draw from specified domains\\n4. **Integration**: System works seamlessly with existing code\\n5. **Testing**: Comprehensive testing shows reduced repetition\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n- Must work with existing ensemble UI system\\n- Should not break current naming functionality\\n- Performance should not degrade significantly\\n- Names should load quickly\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n- Current naming system exists and is modifiable\\n- System uses some form of name database or generation logic\\n- Family-friendly means no offensive, scary, or inappropriate content\\n- Roman political/military terms will be adapted to be whimsical (e.g., \\"Consul Giggles\\")\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. **As a user**, I want to see more varied names so that the experience feels fresh\\n2. **As a user**, I want whimsical names that make me smile and are appropriate for all ages\\n3. **As a developer**, I want the naming system to be easily expandable with new sources\\n4. **As a maintainer**, I want the system to generate consistently high-quality names\\n\\n## Definition of Done\\n\\n- [ ] New name sources implemented and integrated\\n- [ ] Name generation shows measurably reduced repetition\\n- [ ] All generated names pass family-friendly content review\\n- [ ] System maintains existing performance characteristics\\n- [ ] Comprehensive test suite validates name quality and variety\\n- [ ] Documentation updated with new sources and maintenance procedures"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or